<title>POLAND: Poland raises min price of 5-yr bonds to 80.76.</title>
<headline>Poland raises min price of 5-yr bonds to 80.76.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry raised the minimum price of its 12-percent five year bonds, due June 12, 2001, to 80.76 from 80.55 at the last tender of the paper on March 20, the finance ministry said.  </p>
<p>The average price also rose to 80.87 from 80.75 at the last tender.</p>
<p>The ministry accepted 182 million zlotys from among 231 million zlotys worth of bids for the bonds placed against a 300 million zloty offer.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
